cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "School Boards and the Democratic Promise: analysis code and reproduction environment"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the datasets it contains, please cite the
  dissertation. If you use the underlying source records, please also cite the
  archival deposit listed under references.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Knowles
    given-names: Jared E.
    affiliation: Civilytics Consulting LLC
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jknowles/schoolboardsPHD"
abstract: >-
  A study of school board elections in Wisconsin from 2002 to 2012 - who runs,
  who votes, whether it changes anything, and what the upheaval following 2011
  Wisconsin Act 10 did to all three. This repository holds the analysis code,
  the transcribed election panel, and a containerised build that reproduces the
  dissertation's results under the original R 3.1.2 environment, verified
  against the outputs as deposited in 2015.
keywords:
  - school board elections
  - local elections
  - education politics
  - voter turnout
  - candidate emergence
  - Wisconsin
  - reproducible research
  - research compendium
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0   # dissertation text, figures and the deposited PDF
  - MIT         # analysis code and build infrastructure
version: "3.0-modernized"
date-released: 2026-08-23

references:
  - type: thesis
    title: "School Boards and the Democratic Promise"
    authors:
      - family-names: Knowles
        given-names: Jared E.
    thesis-type: "PhD dissertation"
    institution:
      name: "University of Wisconsin-Madison"
    department: "Department of Political Science"
    year: 2015

  - type: data
    title: >-
      Source records for School Boards and the Democratic Promise:
      Wisconsin school board elections, 2002-2012
    authors:
      - family-names: Knowles
        given-names: Jared E.
    year: 2026
    # doi: "10.xxxxx/xxxxxx"   # set once the deposit is published
    notes: >-
      3,995 files, 1.6 GB of scanned canvass statements, clerk responses and
      agency records obtained by public records request. Not required to run the
      analysis; deposited so the analysis remains auditable.
